From dsh-fork-0001 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ddv <ddvnguyen@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 21:15:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fork(web): opt-in fork.allowWildcardHost accepts --host
 0.0.0.0

Stock alpha.5 refuses an unspecified bind address in two places: the web
command-line provider (--host) and the webserver Config. Both stay the default.
A deployment that sits behind an external perimeter and a --trusted-host list
can name `fork.allowWildcardHost: true` on the `web-startup` row; the bundle
passes it on to the `webserver` row, and the Host fence is untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
